jobs.description:
As a Production Worker, no two days are the same! You’ll take on a variety of tasks such as operating the production line, packing and unpacking products, and monitoring progress. Notice a minor malfunction? You’ll take care of it right away. You’ll also make sure that pallets and products are properly labeled and that your workspace stays clean and organized. In addition, there’s an opportunity to work in other departments, making your job even more diverse and dynamic.
 What you can expect from us:
- An attractive gross hourly wage of €15,70;
- A full-time workweek from 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM;
- Do you live outside Zeewolde? You’ll receive a travel allowance of €0.23 per kilometer;
- Work for a stable employer with a pleasant and friendly team atmosphere;
- With good performance, there’s the possibility of a direct contract with the company;
- And of course, you’ll have a dedicated contact person who’s always there to help you with any questions!

 What we ask from you:
- Are you available to start full-time right away? Perfect!
-  You bring a positive attitude and help create a great atmosphere at work;
-  You’re physically fit and enjoy being active throughout the day;
-  You speak good English – if you also speak Polish, that’s a plus;
-  Working neatly and accurately comes naturally to you.

 Do you want to work for a leading family-owned company that has been active in the international market for over forty years?
 Our client in Zeewolde is a true specialist in lighters and produces more than one hundred million consumer packages each year. From natural and barbecue lighters to fluids, gels, and lamp oil – you’ll be contributing to innovative, high-quality products that are distributed worldwide. Will you join this growing and stable company?

In this role, the coordinator will be a key link between the company and its clients, ensuring seamless communication and project execution from the initial inquiry through to final delivery. Working closely with the sales team, this position is responsible for preparing detailed quotes, managing orders, coordinating deliveries, and handling invoicing and payment follow-ups.The role also includes frequent collaboration with international colleagues and direct communication with the headquarters and production sites in the Netherlands to align customer requirements with internal processes.

Here's a list of the specific tasks:- Prepare detailed quotations based on input from Area Managers
- Register and manage incoming orders
- Coordinate logistics and delivery planning
- Oversee invoicing and follow up on outstanding payments
- Act as a primary point of contact for clients, ensuring timely and accurate responses
- Liaise regularly with colleagues across international offices
- Coordinate with the headquarters and manufacturing facilities to meet client expectations
- Maintain a strong focus on customer satisfaction and brand representation

RequirementsThis is a highly autonomous and versatile position that requires both administrative precision and a customer-focused mindset. Next to this, here are some set requirements:
- 3+ years of experience in a similar administrative or client-facing position;
- Professional level of German and English, and an understanding of Dutch (B1+);
- Proficient in Microsoft Office and comfortable working with digital tools;

BenefitsOur client can offer a temporary contract initially, with the intention to continue long-term. Next to this, you would receive:- 25 holiday days (based on full-time);
- Public transport and travel cost reimbursement;
- An open and collaborative work culture;
- Opportunities for growth within an international environment;

